  "chapter": 773,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 92 Chapter 773\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 7537, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the village law and the general municipal law, in\n        relation to establishing the village incorporation commission\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill modifies village incorporation procedures in  several  ways.\nIt establishes a Village Incorporation Commission (Commission) comprised\nof appointees of the Secretary of State, the Comptroller, and the Attor-\nney  General,  who are charged with receiving and reviewing petitions to\nincorporate. The bill,  among  other  things,  increases  the  threshold\nnumber  of  regular  inhabitants  from 500 to 2,000 persons, calls for a\nstudy on the fiscal, tax, service interests of the proposed village, and\nimpacts on the surrounding town, and requires the Commission to evaluate\nwhether the proposed village is feasible in light  of  the  studies  and\nother information.\n \n  I  recognize  the  need  to modernize our village incorporation proce-\ndures.  We want our villages and surrounding towns to be vibrant  commu-\nnities  that  meet  the  needs of their residents. However, the bill, as\ndrafted, required changes to enumerate the procedures for  incorporation\npetition  review  and the elements of the analytical studies, and to set\nthe population threshold at 1,500 persons.  It  was  also  important  to\nclarify  the  scope of the bill's applicability, including that the bill\ndid not apply to petitions where there is a  joint  notice  of  election\nspecifying a date and time of the election and signed by the town clerks\nof  each  affected  town  pursuant  to section 2-214 of the village law,\ndated December 22, 2023 or earlier.\n\n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes.  On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
